# "Died under your control" is about the controller as it died, not the owner (CR 700.4, 109.4). Bot2 owns an Ornithopter (an artifact creature); on turn 3
# Bot1 takes it with Dack Fayden's -2 ("gain control of target artifact"), and Burn Together has it (power 0, so it deals no damage) hit Bot2 and be
# sacrificed. It goes to Bot2's graveyard, its owner's, yet it died under Bot1's control, so the Sell-Sword cast from exile enters with one counter.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Black Lotus
Dack Fayden
Island
Island
Callous Sell-Sword
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Dack Fayden.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Dack Fayden.Activate(Ornithopter; Ability: Gain control)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Callous Sell-Sword.Cast(Ability: Burn Together)
Bot1.Target(Ornithopter)
Bot1.Target(Bot2)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Types = Artifact; Creature
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
? Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
? Exile = Callous Sell-Sword
Bot1.Exile.Callous Sell-Sword.Cast

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Callous Sell-Sword.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Callous Sell-Sword.Power = 3
